      </zones>
      <devicelayouts>
        <devicelayout auto-generated='true' name='Phone'>
          <size maxheight='700' minheight='700' sizing-mode='vscroll' />
          <zones>
            <zone h='100000' id='53' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
              <zone h='98000' id='52' param='vert' type-v2='layout-flow' w='98400' x='800' y='1000'>
                <zone forceUpdate='true' h='86125' id='3' type-v2='text' w='98400' x='800' y='1000'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run bold='true' fontsize='11'>README</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontsize='10'>This report aims to aid with the diagnosis and fixing of data quality issues within Data Streams and CoreData Order models. If you are a platform sending orders, this report should highlight which exact orders are missing or incorrect in some way. We use your Platform DWHs to reconcile what we have available in the central models.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>A few notes</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontsize='10'>- Test orders are excluded (using the Data Streams test_order flag)</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontsize='10'>- CoreData FX Rates are used for EUR conversions</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>Glossary</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontsize='10'>PO = Platform Orders, i.e. directly from the Platform&apos;s DWH</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontsize='10'>OS = Order Stream, i.e. what is available from Data Streams Order stream</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontsize='10'>OSS = Order Status Stream,  i.e. what is available from Data Streams Order stream</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontsize='10'>CDO = CoreData Orders</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontsize='10'>LC = Local Currency</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontsize='10'>EUR = Euros</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontsize='10'>GMV = Gross Merchandise Value (what the customer had to pay)</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontsize='10'>GBV = Gross Basket Value (the value of the basket items &amp; packaging)</run>
                    <run><![CDATA[

Rules are applied in the following order using an ELSE IF logic, so the first broken rule is the rule that is counted for the order
1. Order stream missing order
2. Order Status stream missing order
3. Coredata Orders missing order (that is in the Order & Order Status streams)
4. Order Status stream final success status incorrect (compared to Platform DWH)
5. Coredata Orders success status incorrect (compared to Order Status stream)
6. GBV in local currency <99% correct
7. Delivery Fee in local currency <99% correct
8. Service Fee in local currency <99% correct
9. GMV in local currency <99% correct
10. GMV in EUR <99% correct
11. Incentives total in local currency <99% correct

The code used can be found ]]></run>
                    <run auto-url='true' hyperlink='tabdoc:load-url url=&amp;quot;https://github.com/deliveryhero/datahub-airflow/blob/main/dags/govops/curated_data/sql/order_level_reconciliation.sql&amp;quot;'>https://github.com/deliveryhero/datahub-airflow/blob/main/dags/govops/curated_data/sql/order_level_reconciliation.sql</run>
                    <run>
The resulting data that makes up this report can be found in Data Hub, 
</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Roboto Mono,Menlo,Monaco,Courier New,monospace'>`fulfillment-dwh-production.curated_data_shared_govops.order_level_reconciliation`</run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
              </zone>
              <zone-style>
                <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                <format attr='margin' value='8' />
              </zone-style>
            </zone>
          </zones>
        </devicelayout>
      </devicelayouts>
      <simple-id uuid='{39A79910-CE9D-4B9D-8A94-79A0D5ABD057}' />
    </dashboard>
